  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J6", "U9"],
      "pins": ["J6.A4", "U9.2", "U9.1"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "VBUS"],
      "observed": "On the Microcontroller sheet (mcu.kicad_sch, page 1/4, top-right), the USB-C receptacle J6 VBUS pin (A4) is tied to the VBUS global label (the power-mux output net that feeds the buck) at the same node as the +5V power symbol, instead of being routed to the +5V net that drives U9 (TPS2121RUXR) IN2 (pin 2).",
      "expected": "The specification states the USB VBUS pins go to the +5V net which feeds U9 IN2, and explicitly notes that the mux output net 'VBUS' is 'distinct from the USB +5V net upstream of the mux.' The USB VBUS pin must connect to +5V only, never to VBUS.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "J12 (USB_C_Receptacle_USB2.0_14P) VBUS pins (A4/A9/B4/B9) → +5V net → U5 pin 2/2_1 (IN2)."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "outputs a single OUT ... onto the VBUS net (the board's internal, unregulated/pre-buck rail — note this net is named VBUS in the netlist but is distinct from the USB +5V net upstream of the mux)."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "mcu.kicad_sch page 1/4, J6 USB_C_Receptacle: pin A4 carries the VBUS global label at the same node as the +5V power arrow."}
      ],
      "impact": "The +5V input net and the arbitrated VBUS output net are merged. When powered from the 12 V barrel jack the mux output (~12 V) is driven onto the USB connector's VBUS pin, back-powering/over-volting the host port, while U9 IN2 (+5V) is never powered from USB, so USB-only operation fails. The two rails the spec requires to be separate are shorted together.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic appears largely consistent with the spec (power mux, buck, heater high-side switch, three shared-bus MAX31855 channels, CC pull-downs), but the USB-C VBUS pin (J6 A4) is shown connected to the VBUS global label rather than to the +5V net, merging the mux output with the USB 5V input that the specification explicitly requires to be distinct."
}

